clean_summary:
This is a well-written article I largely agree with. I really dislike it when people pass off AI output as their own, but the section on hallucinations seems flat out wrong. In general, I don't understand how so many people still seem to encounter them.

@QiaochuYuan: "Sam Kriss on AI writing, self-recommending."

The linked article titled 'If you let AI do your writing, I will come to your house and kill you' suggests that it is possible to tell when AI has been used, implying that AI-generated content can be distinguished.

tfw u get ghosted by ur ai assistant...

@interaction: "Say hi to the new Poke! Now officially approved by Apple to text on Apple Messages. As the first and only AI agent. Chat now:"

The linked space describes Poke as a proactive AI assistant on Apple Messages, WhatsApp, Telegram, and more, that texts like a human, really knows you, and integrates with your life in dozens of ways.

Extremely good writing and honestly quite a sad read. Sometimes it's tough to remember, but despite all the anxiety over our future and feelings of lack of control, Americans are in an infinitely better position than the rest of the world.

